{"step_index":1010,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:15:00Z","input_tokens":5823,"cache_read_tokens":436944,"output_tokens":4204,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe student's browser stores a lock in local storage to prevent multiple responses, identified by the quiz ID. This lock is set upon quiz completion and checked on subsequent page loads. Currently, the reset mechanism is limited to a local URL hash or cache clearing. The core challenge is enabling the teacher to remotely reset the lock for all students.\n\n\nThe teacher's ability to globally reset quiz locks hinges on a shared, authoritative state. Introducing a `lockVersion` counter within the Firestore quiz document serves this purpose. Triggering a reset in the teacher's interface increments this `lockVersion`.\n\nWhen the student's quiz loads, it checks against the stored `lockVersion` in the Firestore quiz document. If the student's local lock version doesn't match the Firestore version, the local lock is cleared, allowing a fresh attempt. This system ensures consistent lock management across all student devices.\n\n\nThe optimal location for the reset button requires careful consideration of the teacher's workflow. The teacher is most likely to clear locks during testing, pre/post retakes, or when managing submissions. The `Quiz Options Drawer` offers space, while the `Editor Action Row` provides visibility alongside existing saving tools. The `Submissions tab` might be less intuitive.\n\n\nInitial assessment: placing the reset button within the Quiz Options drawer or alongside the editor action row seems most logical, considering the teacher's potential workflows. Placing a \"Reset Lock\" button, potentially with confirmation, in either location provides accessibility for resetting student locks.\n\nConsideration of teacher action scenarios: a global reset, triggered by the teacher, should update a `lockEpoch` timestamp in Firestore to invalidate student locks. This mechanism ensures all student devices can unlock on reload.\n\n\nThe current implementation prematurely checks for a lock in local storage before retrieving the latest lock epoch from the database. This leads to a sce\n<truncated 2877 bytes>\nmight be null.\n\n\nThe design ensures the \"Download Result File\" button updates correctly when `autoRecordQuiz` is false. The teacher-side interface requires a well-placed \"Reset Student Lock\" button. Considerations for placement: the Submissions tab header, Quiz Options drawer, and the top card row are all candidates, depending on user workflows. The Submissions tab addresses incomplete submissions not yet in the completed list. The key is to provide easy access for clearing student locks whether they started or completed a quiz.\n\n\nThe optimal location for the \"Reset Response Lock\" button appears to be in the main Quiz Editor card action row, alongside the \"Save to Quiz\" and \"Download Quiz File\" buttons. This placement offers high visibility and direct accessibility for teachers managing student responses. The clean, 3-button row using existing CSS classes provides a clear and intuitive user experience. The button will have a confirmation modal.\n\n\n\nThe existing confirmation modal can be reused with a single `pendingConfirmAction` variable to handle \"Clear Students\" and \"Reset Response Lock\" actions. Clicking either button assigns a pending action (`'clearSub'` or `'resetLock'`) to the variable, triggering the confirmation modal. Upon \"Yes\" confirmation, the corresponding function (`purgeRecords` or `resetLockEpoch`) is executed. This approach ensures safety through confirmation while reusing existing UI elements, avoiding extra modal bloat. The double-click-to-confirm is an excellent fail-safe.\n\n\nThe `lockEpoch` is missing in `quizzes/active`, but defaulting to `0` using `Number(data.lockEpoch) || 0` is safe. Triggering the teacher's reset action sets `currentLockEpoch` to `Date.now()`. A direct `PATCH /quizzes/{id}?updateMask.fieldPaths=lockEpoch` updates *only* `lockEpoch` on the remote document, avoiding any unintended changes to the quiz content and preserving any unsaved teacher edits. This RESTful approach is a cleaner, safer fix. It confirms the `updateMask` functionality of the Firestore REST interface.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"firestore rest api patch updateMask document create if missing\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
{"step_index":1011,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:15:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:15:26+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:15:31+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:15:26+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:15:31+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore rest api patch updateMask document create if missing\" returned the following summary:\nIn the Cloud Firestore REST API, the `PATCH` method (`projects.databases.documents.patch`) acts natively as an **upsert**[1]. \n\nBy default, sending a `PATCH` request to a document path will **create the document if it is missing**, or **update it if it already exists**[1].\n\nDepending on whether you want to **merge/update specific fields** or **overwrite the whole document** on creation/update, behavior is managed using the `updateMask` parameter[2]:\n\n---\n\n### Behavior Matrix\n1. **With `updateMask` (Upsert + Merge):** \n   If the document *doesn't exist*, it creates it using only the fields specified in the mask. If it *does exist*, it updates only those specific fields and leaves other existing fields untouched[2].\n2. **Without `updateMask` (Upsert + Overwrite):** \n   If the document *doesn't exist*, it creates it. If it *does exist*, it completely replaces/overwrites the entire document with the payload provided[2].\n\n---\n\n### Example Request (`curl`)\n\nThis example demonstrates how to perform a patched upsert (`create if missing` or `update if present`) targeting specific fields using `updateMask.fieldPaths`[3][1]:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X PATCH \\\n\"https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/databases/(default)/documents/users/user123?updateMask.fieldPaths=name&updateMask.fieldPaths=status\" \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\" \\\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n-d '{\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"name\": { \"stringValue\": \"Alice\" },\n    \"status\": { \"stringValue\": \"active\" },\n    \"ignoredField\": { \"stringValue\": \"This will not be written because it is missing from the updateMask\" }\n  }\n}'\n```\n\n### Key Considerations:\n* **No Preconditions Needed:** Do **not** pass `currentDocument.exists=true` in the query string if you want it to create the document when missing. Setting `currentDocument.exists=true` forces a strict requirement that the document must already exist, which will return a `NOT_FOUND` error if it doesn't[3][4].\n* **Field Path Syntax:** Each field you want to create/update must be explicitly registered as a query parameter using `updateMask.fieldPaths=fieldName`[5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXtuW8bfj6oAaJc_5_yRZd0xnvPyAHCQMuML5w4cEnQsNXbg7cYqmOGwD5UkuNRQDH9b3PEY7L38KshgmNr59eXd0OaKZJXVgiCph60vN_aQXdq98_DsDEw3pyHgRyuN9fMldWFQLyz_Y-ONhKk_0ZvJOpP50Syc_QozCTha7fzK6vhLdS4fX9JVl-B9B_wWVJSpVW)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7irSsfgINDRApK97ub12kBtQb0pCTGvel6bmrHbWEfAYDZIq2EIHp-5ntiSo4mLVaqAuPZzrN07SkVavFqnngtvIWvPsivOfRBNSX9EUT2cN5Xyk_lL4YAIxusUotv7IrQ8FuZOHwSg-5hoz7YRcd-R0xSVcQEia7jNcD)\n[3] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG9AFc4cbqAwLrjJeB1P9zDwO5lUl51IWG_vnu00VVGFyJo5h5XpRm_wAlnSxcyoan-1Jr1utYhbZvtThu9GvwM_fYPEayZIeVB_r8PxHHVKupPc3V0qVdvNC1v-_AFMNbiNqUQEtYDkjqGenS0x7dkGhxNfhzavdahktm3AtbbliyCEj4JKDudbT69HzNBdLgMkkINnMHD7ZumlFsMBaEFy8KZ12rh)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGKBSmKf3MZRfNI2lc0KuCCp3-vQ5MCPFL78EB25CYsoKQmu2qsDRZSV9gApwn-zHgzCkZF_suZsCT3E_7zLbtvBzrYp2sCXhwk9YjEWvqTiM8AssWH8bI9mwn3SZcwF91ETYIEsgO5ABheipUS)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHR-RQJCWFIfgjxYSz9Y1pqJNp2Wf8WAIHokgLeWOmq5BPsbj1LyljeZfV40Vxy1vdO92b864yC-xm8F-T-Ts91XQVHVfALoR94_MDtqVAbOe_b26Oc6eq32RSLwHf_6B4B3IEDY1isXtGIcTBk94NIaewqFnX5wX2gsO1xayexvDew6NUpZDPFpiKhGba1fZqqig==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
