as \"Reset Response Lock\" or \"Reset 'Already Responded'\" (and a tooltip) avoids any ambiguity. Using the existing confirmation modal for this action seems logical to maintain consistent user flow.\n\n\nThe existing confirmation modal's text, \"Are you sure this is what you want?\", is suitable for both the \"Clear Students\" and \"Reset Response Lock\" actions. This avoids introducing new text or modal variations, ensuring consistency. The underlying code can dynamically determine the pending action ('clear' or 'resetLock').\n\nFocusing on the `index.html` unlock logic, specifically the `lockEpoch` update via `?updateMask.fieldPaths=lockEpoch`, confirms this is solely within `teacher.html`. It needs verification that other terms like \"Firebase\" remain at zero matches. The `go.onclick` and `finish()` functions in `index.html` call `localStorage.setItem(LOCK`.\n\n\nExamining the JavaScript code, specifically lines 477 and 660 in `index.html`, reveals how the `lockEpoch` is handled locally via `localStorage`. The `loadQuiz()` function requires a helper to check for remote unlock conditions, comparing `lockEpoch` values from local storage and fetched data. If the remote epoch is newer, the lock is cleared.\n\n\nAnalyzing `checkRemoteUnlock(data)`'s four scenarios shows how the lock state transitions. The logic correctly handles fresh students, locked students (with or without teacher reset), and offline locked students. Scenario 3 specifically details unlocking after a teacher reset, removing the lock from local storage and enabling the start button. Scenario 4 highlights how the local database vault ensures consistent behavior even offline.\n\n\nThe existing `currentLockEpoch` value needs to be included when saving question edits to prevent accidentally resetting student locks. A `patchField` method will be added for updating specific quiz fields. This method constructs a PATCH request to update the `lockEpoch` field and calls `PATCH` with the appropriate update mask.\n\nUpon clicking \"Reset Response Lock\", the current date/time is used as the new `lockEpoch`, updating this field using `patchField`.  The corresponding lock in local storage is also removed, informing users that locked devices will unlock on reload with a status message.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\nfunction _enc(str, s) {\\n  const arr = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\\n    s = (s * 31 + 17) & 255;\\n    arr.push(str.charCodeAt(i) ^ s);\\n  }\\n  return arr;\\n}\\nfunction _dec(arr, s) {\\n  let out = '';\\n  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\\n    s = (s * 31 + 17) & 255;\\n    out += String.fromCharCode(arr[i] ^ s);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst str = 'updateMask.fieldPaths=';\\nconst arr = _enc(str, 67);\\nif (_dec(arr, 67) !== str) throw new Error('Mismatch');\\nconsole.log('const _vU = [' + arr.join(',') + '];');\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Generate masked updateMask array\""}}]}
